From: utzcoz <utzcoz@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:59:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] vr: support NixOS and NVIDIA in the Linux XR sandbox

NixOS puts Vulkan drivers under /run/opengl-driver and /nix/store.
Grant the XR service access to selected driver files and directories,
then preload drivers before seccomp so their dependencies are ready.

Allow NVIDIA's device nodes and driver parameters needed by SteamVR.
Also permit scheduler priority queries and DRM device listing.

Test: in an Ubuntu/AMD RADV container, put Vulkan ICDs and libraries
under /nix/store, link /run/opengl-driver to the profile, and hide FHS
Vulkan files. Run Chromium with Monado and OpenXR enabled; confirm the
VR session renders with the sandbox on.
A NixOS user reports SteamVR/Index renders with the NVIDIA changes.
Native NixOS/NVIDIA was not tested on this host.

Bug: 506004811
